    {
      "original_record": {
        "evidence_refs": [
          {
            "evidence_id": "E-40f674e99a623758",
            "page": 2,
            "source_id": "ntrs-20205007829"
          }
        ],
        "id": "open_question-ntrs-20205007829",
        "text": "Operating in the Lunar Vicinity (proving ground) After 2030 Leaving the Earth-Moon System and Reaching Mars Orbit Now 2020s EXPANDING HUMAN PRESENCE IN PARTNERSHIP CREATING ECONOMIC OPPORTUNITIES, ADVANCING TECHNOLOGIES, AND ENABLING DISCOVERY \uf0d8No matter the mission or the destination, each will present unique fire safety challenges for spacecraft or habitats \uf0d8Spacecraft designers and mission operations personnel will (generally) not realize the extent of the fire safety question they need answered until a solution is needed (quickly) 2",
        "type": "open_question"
      },
      "reason": "legacy epistemic classification has no reviewed publication authority"
    },
    {
      "original_record": {
        "evidence_refs": [
          {
            "evidence_id": "E-af031f03bfd556c1",
            "page": 14,
            "source_id": "ntrs-20205007829"
          }
        ],
        "id": "nasa_conclusion-ntrs-20205007829",
        "text": "What is the perceived risk for a spacecraft fire? \uf0b7 Programs that have conducted probabilistic risk assessments have generally rated the fire risk very low \u2013 Depending on assumptions, risk of Loss of Vehicle by a fire could be on the order of 1 in 300,000 to 1 in 3,000,000 \uf0d8To a Program Manager, low probabilities indicate a fire event is very unlikely \u2013 In some cases, there is no real belief that a fire could occur \uf0b7 This drives decisions that impact how a vehicle program addresses the fire risk beginning in the design phase \u2013 Flammability and material control \u2013 Isolation from ignition sources \u2013 Detection \u2013 Suppression \uf0b7 This trend will probably continue unless we provide a clear set of requirements and/or guidelines that all Programs need to follow 14",
        "type": "nasa_conclusion"
      },
      "reason": "legacy epistemic classification has no reviewed publication authority"
    },
    {
      "original_record": {
        "evidence_refs": [
          {
            "evidence_id": "E-a9fde6c0cd4e5b2d",
